# Punctuation

Never write an em dash (U+2014, the long dash). Use an en dash (U+2013) for breaks, ranges, and title separators.

```text
Wrong: Kagunga Farms Company Limited — Njombe
Right: Kagunga Farms Company Limited – Njombe

Wrong: Fruit is picked for partners — packers and traders.
Right: Fruit is picked for partners – packers and traders.
```

In the wrong lines above, the mark is the long em dash. In the right lines it is the shorter en dash.

Do not use `--` or a hyphen where an en dash belongs. This applies to EN, SW, HTML, JS copy, comments, and generated pages.
